      "notes": "Confirms labialised consonants (kʷ, gʷ, kʼʷ, and the wider Cʷ series written with the dedicated Ethiopic \"wa\" glyphs) are phonemically contrastive in Amharic, not derivable from a /Cua/ or /Coa/ vowel sequence or from /w/-loss alone (Table 2 surveys 100 years of prior analyses)."
